   "subject": "Analyzing detection & density dsing distsamp with multi-year count data",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 6pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Dear unmarked Community,</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:9pt 0pt 6pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">I am reaching out to seek your guidance on the best approach to analyze my multi-year dataset using the unmarked package, </span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:italic;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">distsamp</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">, given some of the challenges I’m currently facing. I have already incorporated some of the advice shared by Ken Kellner (</span><a href=\"https://groups.google.com/g/unmarked/c/9F_i-LwwW-A/m/J-pDaI2xBQAJ\" style=\"text-decoration:none\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/g/unmarked/c/9F_i-LwwW-A/m/J-pDaI2xBQAJ&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792448201190000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0YoZuLcGYTKZ3c2B8_PORq\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(41,98,255);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">a previous thread</span></a><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">) but have encountered issues that I’m hoping to get more clarity on.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:6pt;padding:9pt 0pt 0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Study overview</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">:</span></p><ul style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:6pt;margin-bottom:0pt\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">I am studying a single species of alpine breeding bird in California.</span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Data were collected over five years (2018-2022) using a double-observer approach. I served as the primary observer, with different (but consistent) secondary observers each year.</span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:15pt\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Surveys were conducted as single-visit counts at 216 sites, organized into blocks of 8 points spaced 250 meters apart. Not all sites were surveyed each year, but each was visited at least three times over the five years.</span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:6pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 15pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">This model is meant to build in to spatial analysis where I plan to estimate habitat suitability and predict a distribution and population for the species. </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:6pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Data structure &amp; covariates</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">:</span></p><ul style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:6pt;margin-bottom:0pt\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Detection data: Count data from each survey point, with distances recorded to detected birds.</span></p><ul style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:circle;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Det Covs in best models were: </span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:italic;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">slope</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">, </span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:italic;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">time of day</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\"> (quadratic), and </span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:italic;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">snow</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\"> (measured as % cover in 50m at site)</span></p></li></ul></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Static site covariates: Distance to cliffs, woody vegetation cover, slope.</span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:15pt\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Dynamic site covariate: Annual variation in snow cover measured as a percentage within a 50m radius and distance to the nearest snow patch and distance to nearest snow patch</span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:6pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 15pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Spatial structure</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">: </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">I am analyzing sites (there are 216 sites within 27 blocks). Prior to accounting for imperfect detection with unmarked, I ran a glmm with a neg binom and best modes (based on AIC) had covariates distance to snow, cliffs and water, woody vegetation and ‘block’ as a random factor. blocks consistently had zero detections, which might indicate unsuitable habitat.</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:6pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\"><br></span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:6pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Current approach</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">:</span></p><ul style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:6pt;margin-bottom:0pt\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-style:normal;font-weight:400;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Based on the advice received and current package capabilities, I opted to use </span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\"><b><i>distsamp</i></b></span><span style=\"font-style:normal;font-weight:400;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\"> due to its compatibility with my count and distance sampling data, even though it does not directly accommodate double-observer data, nor does it allow me to have a negative binomial distribution, ZIP, or random factors.</span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-variant:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;font-weight:400;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-variant:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">I used parametric bootstrapping (</span><span style=\"font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-variant:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\"><b>parboot</b></span><span style=\"font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;font-weight:400;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-variant:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">) to assess model fit, which indicated some overdispersion (</span><span style=\"text-decoration:none;font-weight:400;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-variant:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\"><i>c-hat</i></span><span style=\"font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;font-weight:400;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-variant:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\"> values up to 2.14) </span><span style=\"font-style:normal;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-variant:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\"><b><u>→ I have included GOF table at bottom of page</u></b></span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:15pt\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"text-decoration:none;font-weight:400;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Detection probabilities and density estimates varied significantly between years. For example, detection probabilities were sometimes over 100%, and d</span><span style=\"text-decoration-line:none;font-weight:400;background-color:transparent;font-size:12pt\">ensity estimates (km2) are incredibly low as well (possibly because I am using all the zeros - even at sites where the birds were never seen in 3-5 surveys over the course of 5 years </span><span style=\"background-color:transparent;font-size:12pt\"><b><u>→ I have included a table with det probs and density estimates at bottom of this page</u></b></span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:15pt;margin-bottom:6pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Current challenges</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">:</span></p><ol style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:decimal;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:6pt;margin-bottom:0pt\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Handling zero detections</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">:</span></p><ul style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Many blocks consistently had zero detections across all years, possibly indicating unsuitable habitat (that is to say I am analyzing by ‘site’ and so there are a huge number of zeros</span></p><ol style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:lower-roman;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">some of these zeros make sense and are at sites that are within a single ‘block’ (or basin along the transect we surveyed at sites 1-8) and are generally at the lower elevations of the transect (sites 1-8 in a basin were almost always rising in an elevational gradient. </span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:lower-roman;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:underline;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">some of these zeros are zeros at sites 1-8 in a basin every year surveyed (i.e. unsuitable habitat)</span></p></li></ol></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-style:normal;font-weight:400;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Should I exclude these zero-detection sites to improve density estimates or incorporate a site-level random effect for blocks (though </span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\"><b><i>distsamp</i></b></span><span style=\"font-style:normal;font-weight:400;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\"> does not support random effects)?</span></p></li></ul></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:decimal;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Relative Abundance vs. True Density:</span></p><ul style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Since I am using </span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:italic;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">distsamp</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\"> without double-observer adjustments, am I effectively estimating relative abundance rather than true density?</span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">If so, would this approach still support creating reliable habitat suitability maps and distribution models?</span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\" role=\"presentation\">Where we have zeros within a basin (all 8 sites), based on my experience, there is unsuitable habitats – this and the low densities and reliable detection. Would this be better to approach from a true density approach?</p></li></ul></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:decimal;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Integration of double-observer data:</span></p><ul style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-style:normal;font-weight:400;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">I analyzed detection probabilities using MRDS for my double-observer data. My plan is to put these coefficients into my </span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\"><b><i>distamp</i></b></span><span style=\"font-style:normal;font-weight:400;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\"> model to improve detection estimates – though I am still unsure of exactly how</span></p><ol style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:lower-roman;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:italic;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\" role=\"presentation\"><font color=\"#0d0d0d\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">This species is clustered in low densities within occupied habitats; they are very easy to detect and are reliably in the same general location for long periods of time – which can be shown by the match of counts at each site between Obv1 and Obv2 – even when these observations are spaced out in time.</span></font></p></li></ol></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Is there a recommended method to integrate the detection estimates from MRDS into my current </span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:italic;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">distsamp</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\"> analysis?</span></p></li></ul></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:decimal;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Overdisperson (alternaitve pkgs…. </span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:italic;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">gdistamp</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">)</span></p><ul style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Giving my distribution is skewed and GOF results are overfitting slightly, I wanted to try an run my models with NB or ZIP distribution and/or bring in a random factor – this seems only possible if I switch to the </span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:italic;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">gdistamp</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\"> package. </span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">If I use </span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:italic;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">gdistamp</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">, won’t I be violating the assumptions? These breeding birds can be considered a ‘closed popn’ (I think) as they are tied to the nest during the surveys – when they fledge, we stop surveys, so there is not temporary emigration. </span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:21pt\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">And we are doing single site visits each year, even though the second observer lags behind the first observer by about 1hr this is due to logistics, safety and terrain of the alpine. </span></p></li></ul></li></ol><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:15pt;margin-bottom:6pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Specific questions</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">:</span></p><ul style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px\"><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:6pt;margin-bottom:0pt\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Should I exclude sites that consistently had zero detections (within a block, which would involve identify sites that are nested in a single block of non-occupancy), or continue treating each site as independent?</span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Given my dataset, is </span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:italic;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">distsamp</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\"> still the best approach, or should I shift to another function like </span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:700;font-style:italic;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">gdistamp</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\"> for better integration of detection probabilities?</span></p></li><li dir=\"ltr\" style=\"list-style-type:disc;font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre\"><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:15pt\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">If integrating double-observer estimates is possible, how can I do so within the unmarked framework?</span></p></li></ul><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:15pt;margin-bottom:0pt;padding:0pt 0pt 6pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">I greatly appreciate any advice or suggestions you can provide. I know this maybe a lot, and I am close to wrapping up this analysis and need help from the experts to take it across the finish line!</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:6pt;padding:9pt 0pt 0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Please ask clarifying questions!</span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:6pt;padding:9pt 0pt 0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\">Here are the detection probability estimates for the best models of each year and their densities. </span></p><p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"line-height:1.38;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:6pt;padding:9pt 0pt 0pt\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;color:rgb(13,13,13);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;white-space:pre-wrap\"><img alt=\"(p) table.png\" width=\"534px\" height=\"76px\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/unmarked/attach/46ea6334b8fba/(p)%20table.png?part=0.1&amp;view=1\"><br></span></p><p style=\"border:0px solid rgb(227,227,227);box-sizing:border-box;margin:0px 0px 0.5rem;color:rgb(13,13,13);font-family:ui-sans-serif,-apple-system,system-ui,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:16px\"><br></p><p style=\"border:0px solid rgb(227,227,227);box-sizing:border-box;margin:0px 0px 0.5rem;color:rgb(13,13,13);font-family:ui-sans-serif,-apple-system,system-ui,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:16px\">Here is are the results of the parboot GOF tests. Note the high chi-sq values.</p><p style=\"border:0px solid rgb(227,227,227);box-sizing:border-box;margin:0px 0px 0.5rem;color:rgb(13,13,13);font-family:ui-sans-serif,-apple-system,system-ui,&quot;Segoe UI&quot;,Helvetica,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,Arial,sans-serif,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;;font-size:16px\"><img alt=\"GOF_table_best-models.png\" width=\"534px\" height=\"370px\" src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/unmarked/attach/46ea6334b8fba/GOF_table_best-models.png?part=0.2&amp;view=1\"><br></p>"
    ]
